    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0375" n="259" xml:id="pg259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1641.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-05T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 5, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Present this Government’s congratulations to the new President of whose
                    inauguration we have just learned. We wish for Jiménez and his country
                    undisturbed peace, great prosperity and continued progress. We hope that all
                    factions will unite in patriotic support of the Government and enter into
                    friendly rivalry for the promotion of the common good. The Commander of the
                    vessels there will receive from the Navy Department instructions for the
                    maintenance of order and the proper administration of the Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
